{
$schema: "https://docs.renovatebot.com/renovate-schema.json",

// npm 12 flipped the allow-remote default to "none": any dependency
// resolved to a bare tarball URL is refused with EALLOWREMOTE unless
// allow-remote is "all" ("root" only covers direct project edges).
// npm 12 also still misclassifies legitimate registry tarballs as
// type=remote when arborist re-fetches bundleDependencies packages by
// their lockfile `resolved` URL (npa re-parses name@URL and loses the
// registry typing). Upstream bug + npm's own partial patch:
// https://github.com/npm/cli/issues/9796
//
// Observed on dispatch lockFileMaintenance runs (#1441, #1521, #1577):
// site/package-lock.json refreshed fine (no bundled deps) but the root
// lock died re-resolving @tailwindcss/oxide-wasm32-wasi
// (bundleDependencies), every week, forever.
//
// This must stay TOP LEVEL. The sandbox `.npmrc` used for lockfile
// generation is resolved during extraction (`packageFile.npmrc`) from
// repo/manager-level config only; packageRules are never applied at that
// stage. The same rule scoped to a packageRule (PR #12) was accepted by
// the config validator but was a no-op: #1577, the first LFM run after
// #12 merged, failed identically. Verified locally against npm 12.2.2:
// `npm install --package-lock-only` with `allow-remote=all` written to
// the lock dir's .npmrc regenerates the lock including the wasm32 entry.
//
// `npmrcMerge: true` (set at top level in default.json) keeps each
// repo's own .npmrc (e.g. dispatch's `include=dev`) intact — the
// configured string is prepended to the sanitized repo file.
//
// Scope is the Renovate sandbox only — developer and CI installs keep
// the npm 12 default gate. Blast radius inside the sandbox is bounded:
// Renovate never introduces new URL-referenced deps by itself, every
// resolved URL lands in the PR diff for review, and each repo's own
// audit/advisory gates still run against the refreshed lock.
//
// Delete this once npm/cli#9796 is fixed and the fixed npm ships.
npmrc: "allow-remote=all",
}
